{"Concurrent index builds lack per-key singleflight coalescing - narrowed lock scope allows multiple goroutines to redundantly build the same index with only last write winning cache assignment": 0.6969270706176758, "Skipping PostgreSQL test reduces CI coverage for the initialization path being changed - need tracked issue to fix and consider quarantined/flaky test approach instead of skipping entirely": 0.5074195265769958, "Moving Init to constructor is a significant behavioral change - constructor now performs expensive operations (index building) and can fail during startup rather than deferring to first request": 0.4964526295661926, "Calling code may not handle constructor failures appropriately after Init moved to constructor": 0.12265769392251968, "Deployment infrastructure may not account for potentially long startup times from eager initialization": 0.11799062043428421, "Possible circular dependencies that relied on lazy initialization may break with eager initialization": 0.030096830800175667, "Missing documentation of initialization contract change for future maintainers": 0.03111082874238491, "Initialization order reversed - search index now initializes before watcher starts, creating window where events could occur between index completion and watcher startup leading to potential index inconsistency": 0.6835175156593323, "Missing comment explaining safety guarantees of the new initialization ordering (e.g., full rebuild on startup or watch stream replay)": 0.3938111364841461}